          "id": 2372709678,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Adding `expinfo->hf_info.hfinfo.blurb = NULL;` inside the test in `expert_deregister_expertinfo` allows a static string to be used. If a expert `blurb` is pointed to allocated memory in the future then it would not be freed. Better to save more memory now instead of planning for something that might not occur?  \n  \n```\nC:\\Development\\wsbuild64>run\\Debug\\tshark.exe -G fields | findstr /I Expert_Item | find /c /v \"\"\n4088\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
